.SH "NAME"
miktex-luatex \- an extended version of pdfTeX using Lua as an embedded scripting language
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBmiktex\-luatex\fR\ 'u
\fBmiktex\-luatex\fR [\fIoption\fR...] [[\fIcommand\fR...] | [\fIfile\fR]]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This man page is an adaption of the corresponding
TeX Live
man page\&.
.PP
Run the
LuaTeX
typesetter on
\fIfile\fR, usually creating
file\&.pdf\&. Any remaining commands are processed as
LuaTeX
input, after
\fIfile\fR
is read\&.
.PP
Alternatively, if the first non\-option argument begins with a backslash, interpret all non\-option arguments as a line of
LuaTeX
input\&.
.PP
Alternatively, if the first non\-option argument begins with a
\fB&\fR, the next word is taken as the
\fIformat\fR
to read, overriding all else\&. Any remaining arguments are processed as above\&.
.PP
If no arguments or options are specified, prompt for input\&.
.PP
If called as
\fBmiktex\-texlua\fR
it acts as
Lua
interpreter\&. If called as
\fBmiktex\-texluac\fR
it acts as
Lua
bytecode compiler\&.
.PP
LuaTeX
is an extended version of
pdfTeX
with Unicode and OpenType font support, embeded
Lua
scripting language, the
eTeX
and
Omega
extensions, as well as integrated
MetaPost
engine, that can create
PDF
files as well as
DVI
files\&. For more information about
LuaTeX, see
\m[blue]\fBhttp://www\&.luatex\&.org\fR\m[], you can read the
LuaTeX
manual using the
MiKTeX Help Utility
(\fB\fBmthelp\fR\fR\fB luatex\fR)\&.
.PP
All
LuaTeX
text input and output is considered to be Unicode text\&.
.PP
In
DVI
mode,
LuaTeX
can be used as a complete replacement for the
TeX
engine\&.
.PP
In
PDF
mode,
LuaTeX
can natively handle the
PDF,
JPG,
JBIG2, and
PNG
graphics formats\&.
LuaTeX
cannot include
PostScript
or Encapsulated
PostScript
(EPS) graphics files; first convert them to
PDF
using
\fBmiktex-epstopdf\fR(1)\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
When the
LuaTeX
executable starts, it looks for the
\fB\-\-lua\fR
commandline option\&. If there is no
\fB\-\-lua\fR
option, the commandline is interpreted in a similar fashion as in traditional
pdfTeX\&. But if the option is present,
LuaTeX
will enter an alternative mode of commandline parsing in comparison to the standard
MiKTeX
programs\&. The presence of
\fB\-\-lua\fR
makes most of other options unreliable, because the
Lua
initialization file can disable path searching and/or hook functions into various callbacks\&.
.PP
\fB\-\-lua=\fR\fB\fIfile\fR\fR
.RS 4
Load and execute a
.\" --lua=fileLua
initialization script\&.
.RE
.PP
The following two options alter the executable behaviour:
.PP
\fB\-\-luaonly\fR
.RS 4
Start
LuaTeX
as a
Lua
interpreter\&.
.\" --luaonly
In this mode, it will set
Lua\(cqs
arg[0]
to the found script name, pushing preceding options in negative values and the rest of the commandline in the positive values, just like the
Lua
interpreter\&.
LuaTeX
will exit immediately after executing the specified
Lua
script\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-luaconly\fR
.RS 4
Start
LuaTeX
as a
Lua
byte compiler\&.
.\" --luaconly
In this mode,
LuaTeX
is exactly like
\fBluac\fR
from the standalone
Lua
distribution, except that it does not have the
\fB−l\fR
switch, and that it accepts (but ignores) the
\fB−−luaconly\fR
switch\&.
.RE
.PP
Then the regular options:
.PP
\fB\-\-alias=\fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
Pretend to be program
\fIname\fR, i\&.e\&., set program (and memory dump) name to
\fIname\fR\&.
.\" --alias=name
This may affect the search paths and other values used\&. Using this option is equivalent to copying the program file to
\fIname\fR
and invoking
\fIname\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-aux\-directory=\fR\fB\fIdir\fR\fR
.RS 4
Set
\fIdir\fR
as the directory to which
.\" --aux-directory=dir
auxiliary files are written\&. Also look for input files in
\fIdir\fR
first, before along the normal search path\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-c\-style\-errors\fR
.RS 4
Change the way, error messages are printed\&. The alternate style looks like error messages from many compilers and is easier to parse for some editors\&.
.\" --c-style-errors.\" --file-line-error.\" --file-line-error-style.\" error messages: C/C++ style
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-credits\fR
.RS 4
Display
.\" --credits
credits and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-debug\-format\fR
.RS 4
Enable format
.\" --debug-format
debugging\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-disable\-installer\fR
.RS 4
Disable automatic installation of packages\&.
.\" --disable-installer
Specifying this option overrules settings in the
MiKTeX
configuration data store\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-disable\-write18\fR
.RS 4
.\" --disable-write18
.\" --no-shell-escape
.\" \write18 (run a program from within TeX)
Disable the
\fB\ewrite18{\fR\fB\fIcommand\fR\fR\fB}\fR
construct\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-draftmode\fR
.RS 4
Switch on draft mode\&.
.\" --draftmode
luaTeX; doesn\*(Aqt write a
PDF
and doesn\*(Aqt read any included images, thus speeding up execution\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-enable\-installer\fR
.RS 4
Enable automatic installation of packages\&.
.\" --enable-installer
Specifying this option overrules settings in the
MiKTeX
configuration data store\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-enable\-write18\fR
.RS 4
.\" --enable-write18
.\" --shell-escape
.\" \write18 (run a program from within TeX)
Fully enable the
\fB\ewrite18{\fR\fB\fIcommand\fR\fR\fB}\fR
construct\&. It is only partially enabled by default to avoid security problems\&. When fully enabled, the command (which undergoes the usual
TeX
expansions) is passed to the command interpreter\&. The output of the command is not diverted anywhere, so it will not appear in the log file\&. The command execution either happens at
\fB\eoutput\fR
time or right away, according to the absence or presence of the
\fB\eimmediate\fR
prefix\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-halt\-on\-error\fR
.RS 4
Quit after the
.\" --halt-on-error
first error\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
.\" --help
Give help and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-include\-directory=\fR\fB\fIdir\fR\fR
.RS 4
Add the directory
\fIdir\fR
to the
.\" --include-directory=dir
head of the list of directories to be searched for input files\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-initialize\fR
.RS 4
Become the
\fIINI\fR
variant
.\" --initialize
of the program\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-interaction=\fR\fB\fImode\fR\fR
.RS 4
Set the interaction mode\&. Must be one of
\fBbatchmode\fR,
.\" --interaction=mode\fBnonstopmode\fR,
\fBscrollmode\fR
and
\fBerrorstopmode\fR\&. The meaning of these modes is the same as the corresponding commands\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-job\-name=\fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
Set the name of the job (\fB\ejobname\fR)\&.
.\" --job-name=name
This has an affect on the output file names\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-mktex=\fR\fB\fIfmt\fR\fR
.RS 4
.\" --mktex=fmt
Enable
\fIfmt\fR
generation, where
\fIfmt\fR
must be either
\fBtex\fR
or
\fBtfm\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-c\-style\-errors\fR
.RS 4
Don\*(Aqt change the way, error messages are printed\&.
.\" --no-c-style-errors.\" --no-file-line-error.\" --no-file-line-error-style
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-mktex=\fR\fB\fIfmt\fR\fR
.RS 4
.\" --no-mktex=fmt
Disable
\fIfmt\fR
generation, where
\fIfmt\fR
must be either
\fBtex\fR
or
\fBtfm\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-nosocket\fR
.RS 4
.\" --nosocket
Disable the
Lua
socket library\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-output\-comment=\fR\fB\fIstring\fR\fR
.RS 4
Use
\fIstring\fR
for
DVI
file comment
.\" --output-comment=string
instead of date\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-output\-directory=\fR\fB\fIdir\fR\fR
.RS 4
Write output files in
\fIdir\fR\&.
.\" --output-directory=dir
instead of the current directory\&. Look up input files in
\fIdir\fR
first, then along the normal search path\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-output\-format=\fR\fB\fIformat\fR\fR
.RS 4
Use
\fIformat\fR
for job output
.\" --output-format=format
(one of:
\fBdvi\fR,
\fBpdf\fR)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-recorder\fR
.RS 4
Enable the file name recorder\&. This leaves a trace of the files opened for input and output in a file
.\" --recorder
with the extension
\&.fls\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-restrict\-write18\fR
.RS 4
.\" --restrict-write18
.\" --shell-restricted
.\" \write18 (run a program from within TeX)
Partially enable the
\fB\ewrite18{\fR\fB\fIcommand\fR\fR\fB}\fR
construct\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-safer\fR
.RS 4
Disable
.\" --safer
easily exploitable
Lua
commands\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-synctex=\fR\fB\fIn\fR\fR
.RS 4
Generate
SyncTeX
data for previewers\&.
.\" --synctex=n
If
\fIn\fR
is zero, no
\&.synctex
file is created\&. If
\fIn\fR
is negative, the
\&.synctex
file is a text file\&. If
\fIn\fR
is positive, the
\&.synctex
file is compressed with
\fBgzip\fR
and the
\&.gz
file name extension is added\&.
.sp
Furthermore,
\fIn\fR
is interpreted as a bit field:
.PP
Bit 1 (\fIn\fR AND 2)
.RS 4
Don\*(Aqt add the
\&.gz
file name extension\&.
.RE
.PP
Bit 2 (\fIn\fR AND 4)
.RS 4
Activate form support\&.
.RE
.PP
Bit 3 (\fIn\fR AND 8)
.RS 4
Activate better compression\&.
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-undump=\fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
Use
\fIname\fR
as the name of the format to
.\" --undump=name
be used, instead of the name by which the program was called or a
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
%&
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp
line\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-utc\fR
.RS 4
Init
.\" --utc
time to
UTC\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
.\" --version
Show version information and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
The following options are ignored:
\fB−−8bit\fR, \fB−−etex\fR, \fB−−parse−first−line\fR, \fB−−no−parse−first−line\fR
.PP
These are always on\&.
\fB−−default−translate−file=\fR\fB\fItcxname\fR\fR, \fB−−translate−file=\fR\fB\fItcxname\fR\fR
.PP
These are always off\&.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.PP
\fBMIKTEX_EDITOR\fR
.RS 4
.\" MIKTEX_EDITOR
The editor to use when selecting
\fBe\fR
in the error prompt menu\&.
.sp
The value can contain these placesholder:
.PP
\fB%f\fR
.RS 4
The name of the file, which contains the erroneous line of
TeX
code\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB%l\fR
.RS 4
The line number\&.
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fBMIKTEX_TRACE\fR
.RS 4
.\" MIKTEX_TRACE
Comma\-separated list of trace stream names (see
Chapter\ \&9, Trace Streams)\&. If this variable is set, then
MiKTeX
programs will write trace messages into the configured log sink\&.
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBmiktex-epstopdf\fR(1), \fBmiktex-pdftex\fR(1)
